WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.943
(lively, fast-paced music)

00:00:05.953 --> 00:00:07.494
- I'm sure if someone were to look inside

00:00:07.494 --> 00:00:10.055
my window while I'm playing, they probably

00:00:10.055 --> 00:00:14.341
would have no idea
what's going on in here.

00:00:14.341 --> 00:00:16.847
To watch a theremin being played,

00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:20.764
looks really strange. (laughs)

00:00:23.836 --> 00:00:26.135
(electronic music)

00:00:26.135 --> 00:00:28.283
My name's Pamelia Stickney

00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:31.408
and one of the instruments I love to play

00:00:31.408 --> 00:00:32.741
is the theremin.

00:00:33.928 --> 00:00:35.498
(laughs heartily)

00:00:35.498 --> 00:00:37.206
It’s like, what the hell was that?! (laughs)

00:00:37.206 --> 00:00:39.423
I dunno! (laughs loudly)

00:00:39.423 --> 00:00:41.779
So the theremin's a synthesizer,

00:00:41.779 --> 00:00:44.460
and it's a synthesizer
that's not controlled

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.877
with the use of a keyboard, like a piano.

00:00:49.011 --> 00:00:51.571
I'm controlling the
pitches with my left hand,

00:00:51.571 --> 00:00:53.971
and this hand is just
the articulation hand,

00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:54.888
the volume.

00:00:55.925 --> 00:00:58.758
(theremin scales)

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:07.631
It's controlled without
any physical contact.

00:01:07.631 --> 00:01:11.083
(theremin scales at lower pitch)

00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:13.277
And you can make it like a bird.

00:01:13.277 --> 00:01:15.360
(laughs)

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.849
The really big challenge
with the instrument,

00:01:20.849 --> 00:01:24.016
is it's reacting not just to my hands,

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.757
and how they're moving and my fingers,

00:01:27.757 --> 00:01:31.090
it's sensitive as well, you know, to my whole body.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.554
(theremin music)

00:01:34.554 --> 00:01:37.769
I've recorded on an
album of David Byrne's,

00:01:37.769 --> 00:01:40.269
Grace Jones, the Indigo Girls.

00:01:41.139 --> 00:01:43.722
(joyful music)

00:01:45.821 --> 00:01:48.626
It's such a new instrument still that,

00:01:48.626 --> 00:01:50.210
there's nobody who's going to stand there

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.472
and say, "you're not doing it the way

00:01:51.472 --> 00:01:53.505
it's supposed to be done."

00:01:53.505 --> 00:01:57.693
I don't think there's
anything else like it.

00:01:57.693 --> 00:01:59.598
It doesn't relate to anything else

00:01:59.598 --> 00:02:01.015
I've ever played.

